Data owners define how data should be used and shared, while ensuring that all practices align with legal and organizational requirements. They determine who has permission to access, edit, or delete the data. Data owners define data governance policies and appropriate safeguards to protect data from unauthorized access or malicious activity. They are also accountable for ensuring compliance with applicable regulations, such as GDPR, HIPAA, and County-specific data policies.";}s:8:"relation";a:2:{s:10:"references";a:1:{s:21:"glossary:data_steward";b:1;}s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}}s:10:"persistent";a:4:{s:4:"date";a:1:{s:7:"created";i:1744830424;}s:7:"creator";s:11:"Aditya Seth";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:11:"last_change";a:9:{s:4:"date";i:1744830424;s:2:"ip";s:14:"73.235.164.232";s:4:"type";s:1:"C";s:2:"id";s:19:"glossary:data_owner";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:3:"sum";s:7:"created";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:1060;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}}}